Rationale: The claim states that Phil Rudd became the only Australian-born member of AC/DC when Cliff Williams left the band. While it is established that Cliff Williams played bass on AC/DC's third LP and that the LP was released in 1976, the evidence does not confirm who the only Australian-born member was at the time Cliff Williams left. The evidence is insufficient to determine whether Phil Rudd was the only Australian-born member at that point, as no direct information about birthplaces or nationalities of band members is provided in the relevant findings. Further evidence is needed to confirm this part of the claim.
